{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggeiC4CgbsxNEmwdifSA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BJ3C7JtQjEfrEwQFT19noE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-125821__x600c07/work/Wiretap-TheWire-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-125821; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nc=json.load(open('src/credits.json')); I=c['exitInterview']; S=I['sourceInformation']\nS['testing']=\"Playwright smoke runs in Chromium and WebKit (title, story flow to the ending, every investigation screen, attract start/exit, every mission under the attract bot), a scripted tail-then-tackle chase, a fake DualSense for stick inversion and Xbox glyphs, a touch-only emulation, and the AI Hub harness (2 players, 4 players with latency and loss, host-leave, server) which all passed. Not tested: real iOS Safari, a real controller, a real TV, visual review of every scene.\"\nS['usage']=\"Rough estimate only, no meter available: about 1.5M tokens processed (mostly cached input, roughly 120K output), about US$6-10, about 2 hours of session time.\"\nI['testingFeedback']=[\"About 8 issues: the title menu stayed open over missions and attract, tail state leaked between missions, a tail could succeed with no contact, a fake pad was injected too late, toasts overlapped, my first Person constructor was broken, and two hub-harness failures (the briefing screen blocked network sends, and the no-player server copy sent nothing).\",\"None are known to remain. The most serious were the menu over missions and the briefing blocking hub traffic; both would have broken play.\",\"The AI Hub harness, because it found two real multiplayer bugs; running every mission under the attract bot was second.\",\"Node syntax checks: they passed while the game was still wrong at runtime.\"]\njson.dump(c,open('src/credits.json','w'),indent=1,ensure_ascii=False)\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs &&