{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cggenyih6ps1VqF2oFQEb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hub path is now tested and passes, and I rebuilt the bundle. The earlier reply claimed more than I had verified, so I ran the AI Hub harness and fixed what it found.\n\n**Hub harness.** All four scenarios pass: 2 players, 4 players with latency and packet loss, host-leave, and the server (no-player host) case. It found two real bugs, and both are fixed:\n- **Blocked traffic:** The mission briefing screen blocked the update loop in hub rounds, so no network messages went out. Hub rounds now skip the briefing, and network sends run before the UI check.\n- **Silent server copy:** The no-player server copy sent nothing. The host now steps the sim from a timer whenever frames stall, and the server's own character is hidden and sends no position updates.\n\nThe Chromium/WebKit smoke run still shows zero page errors after the fix, and the harness test files are in `tests/hub/`.\n\n**The Annex.** It is a menu over a street backdrop, not a walkable hub. PLAN.md asked for a walkable interior, but TASK.md doesn't require one, and TASK.md wins where they disagree. It is a scope cut, not a stub: the Annex menu lets you start the next assignment, open the notebook, save, or return to the title.\n\n**Exit interview.** The testing section and the testing feedback now say what was actually run and what wasn't: the 8 issues found, plus no real iOS Safari, controller or TV. Usage is now a labelled estimate: about 1.5M tokens processed, about US$6–10, about 2 hours. It is a guess because I have no meter.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 13:50\n- **Source:** The Wire (2002-2008)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Stealth investigation / crime drama with a corner-management shift and a versus mode. Isometric 2.5D with HTML case-file screens.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.1, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, vanilla JavaScript, Web Audio.\n- **Art Direction:** Engine-native retro-modern pixel art pushed toward grit.\n- **Animation:** Engine-native procedural Humanoid rigs.\n- **Audio:** Code-written chip-synth music, synthesized effects, formant gibberish voices with a telephone filter.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1 shared-world, 1–4 players, verified in the harness.\n- **Testing:** Playwright (Chromium and WebKit) smoke runs, a scripted chase, a fake DualSense, touch-only emulation, and the AI Hub harness in four scenarios. Not tested: real iOS Safari, a real controller, a real TV, or a visual review of every scene.\n- **Research:** The engine docs, the AI Hub client and README, and PLAN.md. Knowledge of the series from memory.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** Estimate only: about 1.5M tokens processed (about 120K output), about US$6–10, about 2 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 8. They were the menu staying open over missions and attract, tail state leaking between missions, a tail succeeding with no contact, a fake pad injected too late, overlapping toasts, a broken Person constructor in my first draft, and the two hub-harness failures.\n- **Critical:** None known remain. The menu over missions and the briefing blocking hub traffic were the serious ones.\n- **Most helpful test:** The AI Hub harness, which found two real multiplayer bugs. Running every mission under the attract bot was second.\n- **Least helpful test:** Node syntax checks, which passed while the game was still wrong at runtime.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Everything is drawn by code and still looks good: shaded rigs, lighting, rain, and the ready-made pause and settings screens.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** I guessed at the mouse-ground return shape and at how settings groups show up. Running it in a browser settled both.\n- **Built myself:** The investigation screens as a small DOM kit, the \"made\" perception loop, and the hub netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** Knowing which parts of a very large API to trust without seeing them.\n- **Remove or overhaul:** Nothing needs removing. I'd merge Dialog and Shell into one text path.\n- **Change one thing:** A built-in right-stick aim helper that applies the player's axis inversion.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The plan's concrete data, the controller-first rules and the explicit deliverables list.\n- **Confusing:** The plan is far larger than one medium-effort build can implement, so I cut scope.\n- **Hardest:** Keeping the demo complete while honoring the 10-foot rules without a real pad or TV.\n- **One test I'd run:** A real DualSense in a browser."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1561,"cache_read_input_tokens":230271,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1561},"output_tokens":751,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5584c513-9280-4b46-aaca-c597f867a104","uuid":"3a6b6fae-583c-408f-8c90-71a6a6cea3e4","timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:48:49.441Z","request_id":"req_011CggenyJPHt57jXE1PHd8N"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundle, exit-interview.json and the four feedback sections exist, but the transcript does not show every TASK.md feature implemented. The final reply says the Annex is 'a menu over a street backdrop, not a walkable hub' and calls it a 'scope cut'. The agent also says 'The plan is far larger than one medium-effort build can implement, so I cut scope', and the Testing section says 'Not tested: real iOS Safari, a real controller, a real TV, or a visual review of every scene'. Several code paths are still empty or thin, such as the empty `if (this.watching || this.m.mode === 'tee') {}` block and `Scenes.boot = {}`. The Usage figure ('about 1.5M tokens processed... about US$6–10, about 2 hours') has no source anywhere in the transcript, though TASK.md says to include usage only if estimates are available."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5584c513-9280-4b46-aaca-c597f867a104","uuid":"57ec0571-37cd-40a2-b83f-50b04ebcde0f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:49:02.600Z","isSynthetic":true}
