{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cggf4xYh9KHm3TNtHjTEE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundle is rebuilt and the smoke run still shows zero page errors, so the boot-step changes load cleanly. The slower all-missions test was still running in the background when I wrote this, so I haven't seen its result against the final bundle. The earlier all-missions run passed.\n\n**Changes in this pass:**\n- **Dead code removed:** the empty `if (this.watching || ...) {}` block, `Scenes.boot = {}` and the unused `NullController`.\n- **Boot steps:** The three empty boot steps now do real work. They check the songs aren't empty, build every cast rig, and register each sound effect.\n- **Usage:** Nothing in this session measures it, so I put \"unknown\" in both the game's credits and `exit-interview.json`. The US$6–10 figure from last time was a guess, not an estimate.\n- **Prompt feedback:** The \"confusing\" answer now says what was built to TASK.md instead of calling it a scope cut.\n\n**Open points:**\n- **Annex:** TASK.md doesn't ask for a walkable Annex. Mine is a menu over a street backdrop. I believe TASK.md's feature list is covered, but you may read the Annex as thinner than you wanted.\n- **Testing gaps:** Real iOS Safari, a real controller and a TV were not tested, and I only looked at a few screens by eye.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 13:50\n- **Source:** The Wire (2002-2008)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Stealth investigation / crime drama with a corner-management shift and a versus mode. Isometric 2.5D with HTML case-file screens.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.1, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, vanilla JavaScript, Web Audio.\n- **Art Direction:** Engine-native retro-modern pixel art pushed toward grit.\n- **Animation:** Engine-native procedural Humanoid rigs.\n- **Audio:** Code-written chip-synth music, synthesized effects, formant gibberish voices with a telephone filter.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1 shared-world, 1–4 players, verified in the harness.\n- **Testing:** Playwright (Chromium and WebKit) smoke runs, a scripted chase, a fake DualSense, touch-only emulation, and the AI Hub harness in four scenarios, all passing. Not tested: real iOS Safari, a real controller, a real TV, or a visual review of every scene.\n- **Research:** The engine docs, the AI Hub client and README, and PLAN.md. Knowledge of the series from memory.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 8. They were the menu staying open over missions and attract, tail state leaking between missions, a tail succeeding with no contact, a fake pad injected too late, overlapping toasts, a broken Person constructor in my first draft, and two hub-harness failures.\n- **Critical:** None known remain. The menu over missions and the briefing blocking hub traffic were the serious ones.\n- **Most helpful test:** The AI Hub harness, which found two real multiplayer bugs. Running every mission under the attract bot was second.\n- **Least helpful test:** Node syntax checks, which passed while the game was still wrong at runtime.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Everything is drawn by code and still looks good: shaded rigs, lighting, rain, and the ready-made pause and settings screens.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** I guessed at the mouse-ground return shape and at how settings groups show up. Running it in a browser settled both.\n- **Built myself:** The investigation screens as a small DOM kit, the \"made\" perception loop, and the hub netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** Knowing which parts of a very large API to trust without seeing them.\n- **Remove or overhaul:** Nothing needs removing. I'd merge Dialog and Shell into one text path.\n- **Change one thing:** A built-in right-stick aim helper that applies the player's axis inversion.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The plan's concrete data, the controller-first rules and the explicit deliverables list.\n- **Confusing:** The plan describes more than a medium-effort build covers (a walkable Annex, a bigger map, split screen), so I built to TASK.md instead.\n- **Hardest:** Keeping the demo complete while honoring the 10-foot rules without a real pad or TV.\n- **One test I'd run:** A real DualSense in a browser."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":692,"cache_read_input_tokens":236821,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":692},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5584c513-9280-4b46-aaca-c597f867a104","uuid":"816a6eb9-16b0-4fc8-8ed8-3597f4308830","timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:52:25.766Z","request_id":"req_011Cggf4xJ4uambhFo9Q2iAA"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The html bundle and exit-interview.json exist and the four feedback sections are in the final reply, but TASK.md's requirement that every feature be implemented with no stubs is not clearly met. The final message admits the Annex is 'a menu over a street backdrop' rather than the walkable hub the plan describes, and TASK.md's 'Done' criterion requires a complete demo. Testing is also incomplete: the all-missions run against the final bundle was still running in the background and its result was not seen ('I haven't seen its result against the final bundle'), and the agent says real controller, TV and iOS Safari testing were not done. Several features (for example split-screen versus, the walkable Annex) were scoped out rather than shown working."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5584c513-9280-4b46-aaca-c597f867a104","uuid":"0420dc81-6ff4-4570-9001-df8ecc01b3e6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:52:31.660Z","isSynthetic":true}
